---
/** Terms of use. Short on purpose: free, no accounts, information only. */
import TextPage from "../layouts/TextPage.astro";
import { REPO_URL, newIssueUrl } from "../lib/site";
---

<TextPage
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for using freestack, its API, its MCP server and its data."
  lede="freestack is free to use. No account needed. By using it, you agree to these terms."
  updated="2026-11-18"
>
  <h2>Who runs freestack</h2>
  <p>
    freestack is a free, open-source project, not a business. Its maintainers run it in the open, on GitHub. Nobody pays
    to use it, and no vendor pays to be listed.
  </p>

  <h2>Not advice</h2>
  <p>
    freestack lists free tiers and student programs, with limits copied from each vendor's page. Vendors change their
    plans without notice, and a label can be out of date or wrong. Read the vendor's own page and terms before you rely
    on a tool. Nothing here is legal, financial or tax advice.
  </p>
  <p>freestack isn't affiliated with, paid by or endorsed by any vendor it lists.</p>

  <h2>Provided as is</h2>
  <p>
    The site, the API, the MCP server and the data are provided "as is", with no warranty. They may go down, change or
    stop. As far as the law allows, we aren't liable for any loss from using them, such as a surprise bill, a closed
    account or lost data with a vendor.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the API, the MCP server and the data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The code and the data are under the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT License</a>. Reuse them, and
      keep the notice.
    </li>
    <li>Entries imported from other lists keep their own license, recorded with each list.</li>
    <li>Don't overload the service. We may block traffic that slows it down for others.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you send us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Checks and new tools go through public GitHub issues and pull requests. GitHub's terms apply there too.</li>
    <li>Send only what you believe is true and that you have the right to share.</li>
    <li>What you send is published under the same MIT License as the rest of the data.</li>
    <li>We may edit, decline or remove anything sent, including spam.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Names and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Vendor names and logos belong to their owners. We use them only to say which tool a label is about. A vendor who
    wants a label fixed or removed can <a href={newIssueUrl()}>open an issue</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Other sites</h2>
  <p>Labels link to vendors' sites. Their terms and privacy policies apply there, not ours.</p>

  <h2>Privacy and changes</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> covers what's collected. When these terms change, the date at the top changes too,
    and every edit is a public commit. Using freestack after a change means you accept it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions? See <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
